Package: CASSIA
Type: Package
Title: Ecophysiological Model for Intra-Annual Tree Growth
Version: 0.1.0
Author: Pauliina Schiestl-Aalto (CASSIA), Joanna Simms (Mycorrhizal additions)
Maintainer: Joanna Simms <joanna.x.simms@helsinki.fi>
Description: CASSIA (Carbon Allocation Sink Source Interactions and Allocation)
    is an intra-annual growth model for individual Scots pine trees in boreal
    conditions. It models seasonal organ-level cell growth, sugar dynamics, and
    water balance. Optional extensions include xylogenesis, mycorrhizal
    interactions, and linkage to soil and photosynthesis models (PRELES, p-hydro).
